      <span id="task-count" style="font-size:.72rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--purple-l);width:36px">0</span>
    </div>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem">
      <div>
        <div style="font-size:.67rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:.4rem;text-align:center">CENTRALIZED MEMORY</div>
        <canvas id="cent-canvas" style="width:100%;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid var(--border);display:block"></canvas>
        <div id="cent-label" style="font-size:.65rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--muted);text-align:center;margin-top:.35rem">after 0 tasks: still diverse</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="font-size:.67rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:.4rem;text-align:center">DECENTMEM (private pools)</div>
        <canvas id="decent-canvas" style="width:100%;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid var(--border);display:block"></canvas>
        <div style="font-size:.65rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--green);text-align:center;margin-top:.35rem">specialization preserved ✓</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="display:flex;gap:1.25rem;justify-content:center;margin-top:.75rem;flex-wrap:wrap">
      <span style="font-size:.67rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--muted);display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.35rem"><span style="width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:50%;background:#8b5cf6;display:inline-block"></span>Planner (A₁)</span>
      <span style="font-size:.67rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--muted);display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.35rem"><span style="width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:50%;background:#06b6d4;display:inline-block"></span>Coder (A₂)</span>
      <span style="font-size:.67rem;font-family:var(--ff-mono);color:var(--muted);display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.35rem"><span style="width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:50%;background:#10b981;display:inline-block"></span>Reviewer (A₃)</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<p>This homogenization is not a bug in the data — it is a structural property of shared memory retrieval. When agents all query the same pool and retrieve the same high-similarity pieces, their policies gradually align. The diversity that motivated instantiating multiple agents is quietly erased.</p>
<p>Beyond diversity collapse, centralized memory also imposes <strong>communication overhead</strong> (every write must propagate and synchronize), <strong>privacy risks</strong> (agent-private experience leaks across the system), and <strong>access bottlenecks</strong> that scale poorly as the agent count grows.</p>
</section>

<!-- §02 ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section id="s-design" data-code="design">
<div class="section-no">02 — Dual-Pool Design</div>
<h2>Private Memory with Two Complementary Pools</h2>
<p>DecentMem's answer is radical in its simplicity: <strong>each agent keeps its own private memory, never shared with other agents</strong>. That private memory is split into two pools with complementary roles.</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">decentmem-architecture.svg — per-agent dual-pool structure</span>
    <span class="vp-hint">three agents, each with private E-pool + X-pool</span>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body" style="padding:1rem">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 640 310" style="width:100%;max-width:680px;display:block;margin:0 auto" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
      <!-- Title -->
      <text x="320" y="18" text-anchor="middle" fill="#6b7280" font-size="9" font-family="monospace" letter-spacing="1">TASK INPUT → EACH AGENT ACTS INDEPENDENTLY → LLM JUDGE FEEDBACK</text>
      <!-- Task input arrow -->
      <line x1="320" y1="24" x2="320" y2="38" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#arr)"/>
      <!-- Agent boxes -->
      <!-- A1 -->
      <rect x="20" y="40" width="180" height="150" rx="8" fill="#1a1a2e" stroke="#3b3b5e" stroke-width="1"/>
      <text x="110" y="58" text-anchor="middle" fill="#a78bfa" font-size="8.5" font-weight="700" font-family="monospace">A₁ — PLANNER</text>
      <!-- E-pool A1 -->
      <rect x="30" y="65" width="74" height="60" rx="5" fill="#12121f" stroke="#4c1d95" stroke-width="1"/>
