<p>Fixed exploitation-only routing costs 6.9% on AgentNet vs online routing — evidence that the learned balance, not just the dual-pool architecture, drives the gains. Exploration-only collapses on structured tasks (BBH) where accumulated experience is irreplaceable, but remains competitive on fresh reasoning tasks (AIME).</p>
</section>

<!-- Listen-friendly content -->
<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display: none;" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: DecentMem — Why Shared Memory Homogenizes Multi-Agent Systems</h2>
    <p>Multi-agent AI systems are designed around specialization: a Planner, a Coder, and a Reviewer each bring different strengths. But when all agents share the same memory pool — the dominant design in current systems like MetaGPT and G-Memory — they gradually all retrieve the same memories and adopt the same strategy. This diversity collapse is not a bug; it is a structural consequence of centralized retrieval.</p>
    <p>DecentMem gives each agent its own private dual-pool memory: an E-pool storing past successful trajectories, and an X-pool generating fresh LLM candidates for unexplored strategies. An online router dynamically adjusts how much each agent exploits its history versus explores new approaches, based on stage-wise feedback from an LLM judge. The authors prove two formal guarantees: global reachability (no agent can be permanently trapped by its own past), and O(log T) regret (the routing converges to the optimal balance at the information-theoretically optimal rate). In practice, DecentMem improves accuracy by up to 23.8% over the strongest centralized baseline and reduces token usage by up to 49%, with the largest gains appearing in the most stochastic multi-agent frameworks — exactly where diversity matters most.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：DecentMem——为什么共享记忆会使多智能体系统趋同</h2>
    <p>多智能体AI系统的核心价值在于专业化：规划者、编程者和审阅者各司其职。然而，当所有智能体共用同一个记忆池时——这是MetaGPT、G-Memory等主流系统的默认设计——它们会逐渐检索到相同的记忆、采用相同的策略，最终丧失多样性。这并非偶然现象，而是集中式检索的结构性后果。</p>
    <p>DecentMem为每个智能体提供私有的双池记忆：E池存储过去成功的协作轨迹，X池生成LLM为新情境创造的探索候选。在线路由器根据LLM裁判的逐阶段反馈，动态调整每个智能体的探索与利用比例。理论层面，DecentMem保证了全局可达性（任何智能体都不会被自身历史永久困住），并实现O(log T)的后悔界（信息论意义上的最优收敛）。实验层面，DecentMem在最具挑战性的随机协调框架AgentNet上超越最强集中式基准23.8%，同时减少高达49%的token消耗。</p>
